Issue 1: Multiple Symbol Definitions in Manifold Namespace
Problem
Multiple definitions of sep::quantum::manifold::memory, quantum, cuda, and api between quantum_processor_qfh_common.cpp and quantum_coherence_manager.cpp.
Root Cause
These symbols are likely defined in a header file (quantum_manifold_optimizer.h) without proper inline or extern declarations.
Solution
Modify include/quantum/quantum_manifold_optimizer.h:
cppnamespace sep {
namespace quantum {
namespace manifold {
    // Change from direct definitions to inline declarations
    inline Component memory = Component::Memory;
    inline Component quantum = Component::Quantum;
    inline Component cuda = Component::CUDA;
    inline Component api = Component::API;
    
    // OR move to a single .cpp file with extern declarations:
    // In header:
    extern Component memory;
    extern Component quantum;
    extern Component cuda;
    extern Component api;
    
    // In quantum_manifold_optimizer.cpp:
    // Component manifold::memory = Component::Memory;
    // Component manifold::quantum = Component::Quantum;
    // Component manifold::cuda = Component::CUDA;
    // Component manifold::api = Component::API;
}
}
}
Issue 2: Missing OSL Libraries for Cycles
Problem
Undefined references to OSL functions from Cycles libraries.
Solution
Update the main CMakeLists.txt to ensure OSL libraries are properly linked:
cmake# After line 146 where CYCLES_OSL_LIBRARY is found, add to CYCLES_LINK_ORDER:
set(CYCLES_LINK_ORDER
    ${CYCLES_KERNEL_LIBRARY}
    ${CYCLES_SUBD_LIBRARY}
    ${CYCLES_DEVICE_LIBRARY}
    ${CYCLES_SCENE_LIBRARY}
    ${CYCLES_SESSION_LIBRARY}
    ${CYCLES_INTEGRATOR_LIBRARY}
    ${CYCLES_OSL_LIBRARY}  # Add this if not present
)

# Add OSL libraries to EXTERNAL_LINK_ORDER after line 200:
list(APPEND EXTERNAL_LINK_ORDER
    ${OSL_EXEC_LIBRARY}
    ${OSL_COMP_LIBRARY}
    ${OSL_QUERY_LIBRARY}
    ${OSL_NOISE_LIBRARY}  # If available
)
Issue 3: CUDA Symbols Not Found
Problem
CUDA symbols from sep::cuda namespace are undefined despite being in .cu files.
Solution
The issue is the linking order. Update main CMakeLists.txt line ~287:
cmake# Ensure sep_compat is linked BEFORE other libraries that use it
if(CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_ID MATCHES "GNU|Clang")
    target_link_libraries(sep_engine
        PRIVATE
        # First link CUDA-dependent libraries
        sep_compat  # Move this BEFORE other SEP libraries
        
        # Then Cycles with whole-archive
        -Wl,--whole-archive
        ${CYCLES_LINK_ORDER}
        -Wl,--no-whole-archive
        
        # OSL must come after Cycles
        ${OSL_EXEC_LIBRARY}
        ${OSL_COMP_LIBRARY}
        ${OSL_QUERY_LIBRARY}
        
        # Then remaining internal libraries
        sep_api
        sep_memory
        sep_quantum
        sep_core
        sep_audio
        sep_blender
        
        # External dependencies
        ${BLENDER_LINK_ORDER}
        ${EXTERNAL_LINK_ORDER}
        ${CURL_LIBRARIES}
        ${HIREDIS_LIBRARIES}
        ${CUDA_LIBRARIES}
        Threads::Threads
        fmt::fmt
        spdlog::spdlog
    )
endif()
Issue 4: Missing createQuantumProcessor Function
Problem
undefined reference to 'sep::quantum::createQuantumProcessor'
Solution
Add to src/quantum/CMakeLists.txt:
cmake# Ensure processor.cpp is included in the quantum library
add_library(sep_quantum STATIC
    evolution.cpp
    pattern_processor.cpp
    processor.cpp  # Verify this is present
    qbsa.cpp
    qfh.cpp
    quantum_processor_qfh_common.cpp
    stabilization.cpp
    types_serialization.cpp
)
Then verify the function exists in src/quantum/processor.cpp:
cppnamespace sep {
namespace quantum {

// This function MUST be defined (not just declared)
std::unique_ptr<QuantumProcessor> createQuantumProcessor(
    const QuantumProcessor::Config& config) {
    // Implementation should be here
    return std::make_unique<QuantumProcessorImpl>(config);
}

} // namespace quantum
} // namespace sep
Issue 5: Missing shutdownLogging Function
Problem
undefined reference to 'sep::logging::Manager::shutdownLogging()'
Solution
Add to src/core/logging.cpp:
cppnamespace sep {
namespace logging {

// Add the missing implementation
void Manager::shutdownLogging() {
    // Implement shutdown logic
    if (logger_) {
        spdlog::shutdown();
        logger_.reset();
    }
}

} // namespace logging
} // namespace sep
Also ensure logging.cpp is added to src/core/CMakeLists.txt:
cmakeadd_library(sep_core STATIC
    allocation_metrics.cpp
    dag_graph.cpp
    engine.cpp
    error_handler.cpp
    logging.cpp  # Add this line
    manager.cpp
    metrics_collector.cpp
    prometheus_exporter.cpp
    tracing.cpp
)